# /etc/valuescan/alert.env - where the alerts go. ROOT ONLY (0600): systemd reads it for
# valuescan-health.service and valuescan-offsite.service before they drop to their users.
#
# Not rendered by bootstrap.sh and never in git: deploy/server/bin/telegram-setup.sh writes
# it (it asks for the token without echo, finds the chat id, sends a test message).
#
# The bot's token from @BotFather (digits, a colon, 35 letters). A SECRET.
ALERT_TELEGRAM_TOKEN=
# The chat the bot writes to: the owner's private chat with the bot, or a group's id
# (negative). Not a secret; the same on both servers and in the GitHub secret
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID (.github/workflows/uptime.yml).
ALERT_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
